From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LAB ONLY: rdpCaptureGfxPro: fill partially damaged tiles from
 the framebuffer

fastrdp backlog A9: X11 desktops over GFX with RemoteFX Progressive
leave stale or wrong rectangles after moving windows; H.264 is clean.
For a 64x64 tile that is only partly damaged, the progressive capture
zero-fills the whole YUVA tile (Y=U=V=0: with the +128 chroma offset a
saturated dark green) and converts only the damaged rects into it; the
encoder then compresses the whole tile with loss, and the quantization
error of the green part reaches the visible pixels near the damage
edges. Window moves produce many such tiles. The H.264 capture
(rdpCaptureGfxA2) has no zero-fill.

This build converts the whole tile from the framebuffer instead (only
the part beyond the screen edge stays zero); the region rects are
unchanged. Clean output points at the zero-fill, the same glitches at
something else (the tile skip: patch 0001, or the encoder).

Diagnostic only: a little more conversion work per partial tile. Not
for production and not in the fastrdp-xrdp package; built only with
the Ansible build method and fastrdp_xorgxrdp_lab_gfxpro_fill_tiles:
true. Applies with or without 0001.
---
 module/rdpCapture.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/module/rdpCapture.c b/module/rdpCapture.c
--- a/module/rdpCapture.c
+++ b/module/rdpCapture.c
@@ -1021,6 +1021,7 @@
     uint64_t crc;
     int num_crcs;
     int mon_index;
+    BoxRec screen_rect;
 
     LLOGLN(10, ("rdpCaptureGfxPro:"));
 
@@ -1094,10 +1095,16 @@
                     rects = REGION_RECTS(&tile_reg);
                     num_rects = REGION_NUM_RECTS(&tile_reg);
                     crc = wyhash((const void*)rects, num_rects * sizeof(BoxRec), crc, _wyp);
+                    /* fastrdp LAB ONLY (backlog A9): the whole tile from the
+                     * framebuffer, not only the damaged rects over zeros; only
+                     * the part beyond the screen edge stays zero */
+                    screen_rect = rect;
+                    screen_rect.x2 = RDPMIN(screen_rect.x2, id->width);
+                    screen_rect.y2 = RDPMIN(screen_rect.y2, id->height);
                     rdpCopyBox_a8r8g8b8_to_yuvalp(clientCon, x, y,
                                                   src, src_stride,
                                                   dst, dst_stride,
-                                                  rects, num_rects);
+                                                  &screen_rect, 1);
                     crc_dst = dst + (y << 8) * (dst_stride >> 8) + (x << 8);
                     crc = wyhash((const void*)crc_dst, 64 * 64 * 4, crc, _wyp);
                     rdpRegionUninit(&tile_reg);
